---
title: Quick Skillet Käsespätzle
description: Hearty and comforting German cheese spätzle made in one skillet with caramelized onions, melted mountain cheese, and sour cream.
servings: 2
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 15 minutes
tags:
  - mains
  - german
  - vegetarian
  - pasta
  - quick
source: https://www.einfachkochen.de/rezepte/kaesespaetzle-einfach-schnell-mit-fertigspaetzle
---

= Sauté the Onions

Halve, peel, and finely dice the @onions{2}(medium) on a #cutting board{} with a #chef's knife{}.

Heat the @sunflower oil{2%tbsp} together with the @unsalted butter{40%g} in a #large skillet{}. Once the butter has melted, add the diced @onions{} and sauté over medium heat for about ~{5%minutes} until translucent and just starting to turn golden brown.

= Melt the Cheese

Add the @fresh spätzle{500%g}(chilled store-bought) to the #large skillet{} and scatter the @mountain cheese{200%g}(grated, or Emmental) over the top. Gently fold everything together with a #wooden spoon{} until the cheese melts and coats the noodles.

Once the cheese has melted, stir in the @sour cream{2%tbsp} and season to taste with @fine sea salt{1/2%tsp}, @black pepper{1/4%tsp}(freshly ground), and @ground nutmeg{1%pinch}(freshly grated).

= Rest and Garnish

Cover the #large skillet{} with a #lid{} and let the spätzle rest over low heat for ~{5%minutes} so the flavors meld.

Meanwhile, wash and shake dry the @fresh parsley{2%tbsp}(or chives), pluck the leaves from the stems if needed, and finely chop. Scatter the chopped herbs over the Käsespätzle just before serving.

> Tip: Crispy fried onions make a wonderful topping for Käsespätzle. Warm store-bought or homemade crispy onions in the oven for a few minutes and scatter them over the dish right before serving.
